# StreamForge AI does not read secrets from .env at runtime.
# Platform credentials are entered in the app (Account Connections) and stored in
# Windows Credential Manager under the service name "StreamForge AI".
#
# Developer-app credentials you enter (secrets::APP_KEYS):
#   kick.client_id / kick.client_secret
#   youtube.client_id / youtube.client_secret     (Google OAuth client, type Desktop app)
#   tiktok.client_key / tiktok.client_secret
#   meta.app_id / meta.app_secret
# Sign-in tokens the app writes itself: kick.token, youtube.token, tiktok.token, meta.token
# OAuth redirect URL to register with Kick, TikTok and Meta: http://localhost:47821/callback
#
# Planned: llm.api_key (Phase 3, moment scoring and metadata)
#
# Optional build-time variables:
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=   # only needed once auto-update is enabled (Phase 7)
